(gc-auto!) resolves to a native C runtime implementation, which the
tree-walking interpreter cannot run ("inline-C not supported in interpreter
mode").  The TI7 inline-c carve-out in run-turi.sh cannot auto-detect this
fixture because the native code is behind the builtin form, not a ```c block
in the fixture or a one-level (load ...) -- hence this explicit marker.
What the fixture pins (a graduated experiment's --enable is a TUR-W0063
no-op, not TUR-E0310) is asserted on the compiled path by run.sh.
